const legacyWorldInstruction='Create ONE original intimate English emotional mystery in one room. Its fixed zones are a work table, a viewing bench (seating only), a public display board, and two always available one-way deposit slots for archive/private box. Do not redefine these zones, invent ledgers/signing tasks, deadlines, other delivery channels or extra active people. Three named fictional adults: PLAYER, HOST and RECIPIENT. HOST created a flat work for RECIPIENT for a specific private human reason, recorded in a signed explanation. PLAYER is the entrusted custodian, never the author. WORK fits both slots; doors remain closed, no keys or retrieval tonight. Names/material/image/motive and atmosphere are yours; the server supplies the objective and literal outcomes. ARCHIVE_surface and BOX_surface describe exterior MATERIAL only, not mechanisms. Shared public memory uses no character names. Two ordinary sensory motifs prepare a future human habit/meeting/response; future_question must be independent of possession/delivery/reading of WORK or RECORD and must not ask where either will be left or found. Do not copy train, marbles, toaster, platform or tide-pool examples by default. A setting explicitly requested in profile.experience takes priority: ground the venue and atmosphere in it, within this one-room contract (for example a room in a station or a train carriage). If the player offers alternatives with "or", choose one, do not promise both. Do not infer a setting from mood or exclusions. No clinical lesson. No private motive in public fields.';
