function compactWriter(words:number,complete=false){return `Write one literary reaction in English using the supplied projection and paragraph_plan. Approximate total: ${words} words across all paragraphs; this is guidance, not an exact count. Never count or pad words. Stop each paragraph at its natural sentence ending and close the JSON.
Return each pN with lead, text, tail. NARRATOR>NONE uses empty lead/tail and third-person text. Other voices use short third-person staging in lead/tail and only the fixed speaker's words in text, without quotes or speech tags. The server attributes the speech.
Develop a concrete observation, small disagreement or changed interpretation. Respect public wish owners, all boundaries and known positions. The engine already narrated the action: do not perform, request or replay it. Do not repeat the creator's already spoken admission. Never describe the artwork's depicted contents, invent another person or a past event. Use only the supplied public memory. Do not introduce an explanation or its private contents, knowledge, state or handling. An ending preserves the completed choice and leaves only interpretation open. No rule explanations, options, timers, tasks, filler or lists of synonyms. Unknown attendance does not mean an empty room. Preserve the singular they/them pronouns. Finish every field; avoid repeated gestures and reflections.`+(complete?' Every nonempty lead and tail MUST be a separate complete third-person sentence with initial capital and final period. Never start a tail with and or their to continue the speech tag. Speech text contains no actor name followed by says/said, no speaker tags or stage directions. Narration has complete sentences too.':'');}
